{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791049909,"nonce":"ki7bAwKeRxzPHeU/bLJZcsypOYI=","title":"Wrong-answer triage: per-enum nullary singletons, EReg/filesystem throws, Dynamic null equality, generic enum ctors","message":"Triage of 32 uncovered wrong-answer rows (four read-only batches). Fixed here:\n\n- Nullary constructors of payload enums are one cell per (enum, tag), registered for reflection; Type.allEnums, createEnum and createEnumIndex hand out the same cells, so `Type.allEnums(E)[0] == A` holds. The previous cell was shared by tag across all enums, which reflection could not tell apart. Issue7209.\n- `EReg.matched(n)` with a group outside the pattern throws \"Invalid group\". Issue6145.\n- `FileSystem.deleteFile`/`deleteDirectory` throw on failure instead of only logging. Issue5742.\n- `target.sys` is defined alongside `sys`. Issue8032.\n- Dynamic `==`: a box of a null String/Array equals a raw null (Issue7536); an unboxed enum's first constructor (discriminant 0, null payload) is not null (Issue6285). A raw object's header can read as a class-tagged box, so only String/Array/Null tags count on the raw-null path (Issue12058/Issue3516 kept).\n- Enum constructors with their own type parameters (`Cons\u003cX, L\u003e(x:X, l:L)`) parsed as junk constructors (`\u003c`, `X`, `\u003e`); the parameters are parsed and erased to Dynamic in the argument types. Issue4578.\n- A concrete scalar passed to a `Null\u003cT\u003e` formal is boxed at the call boundary (does not yet reach the inlined calls of Issue3094/Issue4842, 7d63486).\n\nGate: 816 -\u003e 823, 0 lost, 0 moved; suite 206/0/2; fixtures, integration tests, clippy, runtime tests clean.\n\nRemaining causes filed as cbfd9ab..7ada8ec.","files":null}]}